# Copy to .env and fill in real values. .env itself is gitignored.

# FRAUD_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://fraud:fraud@localhost:5432/fraud_detection

# Supabase (public demo deploy target only -- see SETUP.md "Database
# (Postgres + Alembic)"). Leave unset for local dev; local dev defaults to
# the local Docker Postgres connection string above with zero config.
# SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>:6543/postgres
# SUPABASE_DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres:<password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# Stripe test mode only (see SETUP.md "Stripe (test mode)"). Get these from
# the Stripe Dashboard in Test mode -- never paste live keys here.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# --- Docker Compose (full local stack: `docker compose up`) ---
#
# This is a DIFFERENT, SMALLER list than everything above -- the Compose
# stack (docker-compose.yml, Phase 11) is deliberately self-contained and
# never talks to Supabase. Nothing new needs to be added to THIS file for
# `docker compose up` to work: the three vars above (FRAUD_DATABASE_URL,
# SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL, SUPABASE_DIRECT_URL) are hardcoded directly in
# docker-compose.yml's `backend` service instead of read from here --
# FRAUD_DATABASE_URL always points at the Compose-internal `postgres`
# service, and the two SUPABASE_* vars are force-set to an empty string
# there, specifically so this stack can never accidentally point at Supabase
# even if you've uncommented those same two lines above for an unrelated
# host-based test.
#
# The only vars from THIS file the Compose stack actually reads are the
# three Stripe ones above (via docker-compose.yml's `backend.env_file`,
# which loads this file directly, and the `frontend` build arg
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, which reuses STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# above rather than needing a second, differently-named copy) -- all three
# are optional; leave them commented out and the stack still runs correctly,
# with Stripe-dependent endpoints returning a clean 503 instead of an error.
#
# First-time setup once `docker compose up -d --build` is running:
#   docker compose exec backend alembic upgrade head
# (see docker-compose.yml's own comment above the `backend` service for why
# this is a manual step rather than an automatic one, and when you need to
# re-run it.)
